// Title: Exchange PowerShell Snap-Ins Usage
// ID: 25676e10-2121-446e-80a4-71ff8506af47
// Status: test
// Level: high
// Author: FPT.EagleEye, Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-03-03
// Tags: attack.execution, attack.t1059.001, attack.collection, attack.t1114
// Description: Detects adding and using Exchange PowerShell snap-ins to export mailbox data. As seen used by HAFNIUM and APT27
// Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

process where (((process.command_line like "*_Add-PSSnapin*") and (((process.executable endswith "\\powershell.exe" or process.executable endswith "\\pwsh.exe")) or ((process.pe.original_file_name == "PowerShell.EXE" or process.pe.original_file_name == "pwsh.dll"))) and ((process.command_line like "*_Microsoft.Exchange.Powershell.Snapin*" or process.command_line like "*_Microsoft.Exchange.Management.PowerShell.SnapIn*"))) and not ((process.parent.executable == "C:\\Windows\\System32\\msiexec.exe" and process.command_line like "*_$exserver=Get-ExchangeServer ([Environment]::MachineName) -ErrorVariable exerr 2> $null*")))
